// bubbler profile: lutris
//
// Lutris itself is a GTK app, but every Wine or Proton game it starts is
// an X11 client — Wine's X11 driver takes precedence over its Wayland one
// whenever DISPLAY is set (Arch wiki, Wine#Wayland) — so this profile
// grants `x11 "host"`, with the isolation caveat that carries: X11
// clients can keylog and inject into each other. The nested server
// bubbler starts by default has no window manager, which is what a game
// that maps and resizes its own windows expects.
//
// `wayland` is Lutris's own display, not the games': its window is a
// native Wayland client here (measured: the compositor reports it with
// `xwayland` false), so it draws through bubbler's proxy and a security
// context, which the X11 socket beside it gives nothing like.
//
// `dri` is the GPU the games render on, and the GL Lutris asks for
// itself: without it the window still maps, but every GLX context fails
// (measured: BadValue from X_GLXCreateNewContext). Bare, not
// `kms=#true`: a game drawing into a window on this session's compositor
// is not the display controller, and `kms=#true` would leave the card
// sysfs — the monitors' EDID and modes — readable on top. What bare
// `dri` binds anyway on the proprietary NVIDIA driver, whose EGL will
// not take a Wayland display without the primary node, `lint` notes.
// Gamescope wants a card node only as an embedded compositor; a Wine
// manager runs it nested, as a client of the session (Arch wiki,
// Gamescope).
//
// `network` is the sandbox's own network namespace, for the runners,
// the Proton and DXVK builds and the installer scripts Lutris fetches.
// `gamepad` is the controllers a game reads through evdev, and it binds
// /dev/input whole: the keyboard and the mouse of this seat come with
// it (measured: the nodes readable inside are the ones udev gave this
// login an ACL on). Drop the node for a game that needs neither.
//
// Sound is `pulseaudio`. The grant binds $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pulse/native —
// the socket PipeWire's pulse server holds on a PipeWire host — and sets
// PULSE_SERVER to it, which is the path a libpulse client takes, as Wine
// and the Proton runtimes are. Bare, it is playback only: no microphone,
// no other app's audio — not the sink's monitor either — and the
// private server it now runs behind refuses to load a module, with the
// policy installed, which is the drop-in and the linking hook it loads;
// `lint` warns `audio-policy-missing` where it is not. Not measured here: if a
// game is silent, add `pipewire` beside it.
//
// umu, Proton and DXVK's 32-bit path make i386 syscalls; the default
// filter carries i386 as well as x86_64, so they are filtered rather than
// killed. Never add `userns "disable"` — those runtimes nest
// pressure-vessel's own bubblewrap.
//
// ~/Games is Lutris's own convention for the install directory. The
// share is `optional`, so a host without one is not a failed run: the
// bind is skipped (`--explain` says `absent on this host, skipped`) and
// Lutris installs into the private home's own Games directory instead.
// Create ~/Games to share a library you already have, or edit the node
// to the directory you keep one in. A prefix or library outside the home
// is named explicitly, e.g.
//   path-share "/kioxia/Games" mode=rw
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dbus {
//       own "net.lutris.Lutris"
//       talk "com.feralinteractive.GameMode"
//       talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
//   }
//     — Lutris's own name (a second `lutris` and the lutris:// handler
//       reach the running one through it), the GameMode daemon, which
//       simply resolves to nothing where gamemoded is not installed, and
//       the screensaver blocker a running game holds.
//   portals
//     — Lutris calls the portals itself, for the file chooser among other
//       things. Not measured: a Proton or umu game brings
//       pressure-vessel, the same steam-runtime-tools that refuses to run
//       where /.flatpak-info exists (see `steam`), so this grant is also
//       what to drop first if a game stops with a Flatpak complaint.
//       Needs `dbus`.
//   system-bus {
//       see "org.freedesktop.UDisks2"
//       call "org.freedesktop.UDisks2=org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager.GetManagedObjects@/org/freedesktop/UDisks2"
//   }
//     — the drive list Wine builds from UDisks2: `see` plus that one
//       ObjectManager call, and no more. A `talk` there would reach loop
//       setup, mount and LUKS unlock, which polkit judges as you.
//   notify
//     — install and download notifications. Needs `dbus`.
//   tray
//     — the tray icon. Needs `dbus`.
//   pipewire
//     — a game speaking PipeWire itself, and the screen-share portal.
lint-allow "x11-without-reason" reason="Wine and Proton games are X11 clients that want a window manager; a nested x11 with wm= is the alternative"
wayland
x11 "host"
dri
pulseaudio
network
gamepad
home-share "Games" mode=rw optional=#true
desktop "net.lutris.Lutris.desktop"
command "lutris"
